diff --git a/BUILD_LOG.md b/BUILD_LOG.md
index 3fea824b..6711642b 100644
--- a/BUILD_LOG.md
+++ b/BUILD_LOG.md
@@ -1360,3 +1360,100 @@ Changes (worker, api, web; migration 0085):
 * Full suite 5087 passed after the two gate fixes above; web tsc, eslint and vitest green.
   Rolled out as rel-b8be0b8 (api 00089, worker 00068, web 00050; migrate job ran 0085), then the
   gate fixes as the tag recorded in the staging memory note.
+
+## 2026-10-31: raw workspace ZIP import boundary
+
+Implemented the first Phase 2 slice of the workspace parity work:
+
+* `exports.repair.ingest` inspects bounded ZIPs in memory, never extracts or executes archive
+  scripts, rejects traversal/duplicate/non-regular/encrypted/oversized/high-ratio members, checks
+  CRC integrity, and inventories JSON arrays, workbook sheets/rows/header candidates and document
+  headings/tables.
+  It deterministically reads the supported subset of `RESTORE.md`, a conventional company record,
+  and validated `checked.json`, `stack_names.json`, and `drop_*.json` build inputs with source-path
+  provenance. It statically parses only literal platform dictionary, stack-lane and people-lane
+  assignments from allowlisted Python files; dynamic expressions are not evaluated, and ambiguous
+  duplicate inputs are reported rather than selected. Duplicate JSON keys and excessive nesting
+  are refused/reported.
+* Added the account-scoped `POST` and `GET /v1/accounts/{domain}/workspace-imports` endpoints.
+  The upload is streamed with a 100 MB cap, bound to the selected account, stored under that
+  account's erasable object prefix, version-serialized on the account row, and private to its owner
+  under forced tenant-and-owner RLS. A reported company-domain mismatch is rejected. Results are explicitly
+  `incomplete` until the remaining config/pipeline rules are derived; no archive script is run.
+* The account page now has a ZIP import panel with version history and a clear inspection-only
+  state. OpenAPI and generated TypeScript contracts were refreshed.
+* The delivered parity screen now returns backend-calculated `computed_summary`, a backend
+  `summary_mismatches` result against the workbook manifest, and the server's people-lane order.
+  The frontend renders these fields and no longer receives the row projections it used to count
+  jobs/people/ranks locally.
+* Added `parity.compare_workspace` and a content-free golden diff report. The exact BD RESTORE
+  sequence completed in a Bubblewrap sandbox with no network, no host home/secrets and only
+  read-only dependency/source mounts. Summary, Evidence, People and Tech match; Jobs has two
+  `Full description` cell differences at `Jobs!M81` and `Jobs!M98`.
+* Follow-up checks: importer/config tests 16 passed; golden comparer tests 2 passed; the BD extracted
+  config validated against both its JSON Schema and Pydantic model. The runtime import count was 366
+  files with zero validation issues, five deliverables, 31 ranked platforms, three checked
+  platforms, 188 stack names, six drop pairs, seven stack-lane mappings and eight people lanes.
+* Tests: synthetic inspection/config/storage/write-owner suites: 18 passed; route catalog,
+  backend count tests: 10 passed; parity UI tests: 3 passed; Postgres import/parity service tests:
+  5 passed on a fresh scratch database; the RLS catalog query returned `[]`; migration `0098`
+  downgraded to `0097` and upgraded again successfully. Route catalog, OpenAPI snapshot,
+  generated client, TypeScript, targeted ESLint and Ruff passed. Alembic history resolves
+  `0097 -> 0098`.
+* Non-executing reference inspection of `/home/sakib/Downloads/BD_workspace.zip` found 366 files,
+  all five deliverables and zero validation issues. It derived three checked platforms, 188 stack
+  names, six false-positive drops, 31 ranked platforms, seven stack-lane mappings and eight people
+  lane names from the named static inputs with source-path provenance.
+* Limits observed: migration lint passes on `0098` alone and reports only the existing unannotated
+  SECURITY DEFINER at `0096_purge_deleted_account.sql:152` when scanning the whole migration
+  directory; earlier migration files were left untouched. Full isolation suite has not run.
+  `docs/workspace_parity.md` records current status and remaining work.
+  The web suite ran 293 passed / 1 failed: existing `documents.test.tsx` expected `indexed` but
+  received `parsed`; this is outside the new import component and has not been baseline-compared.
+  A broader parity workbook test passed 41 / skipped 1 but its rendered-workbook case failed when
+  the LibreOffice subprocess exited 1; its stderr was unavailable in the sandbox.
+* Next: extend contract extraction from notes/build inputs, port the remaining legacy config-driven
+  rules, then wire deterministic canonical queries and raw imports into the rendered parity views.
+
+## 2026-11-01: imported deliverable views and client-only export
+
+* `exports.repair.views` now creates bounded structured views for the imported Summary, Evidence,
+  People, Jobs and Tech deliverables. Workbook parsing caps rows, columns, cell text and aggregate
+  serialized view size. DOCX extraction retains paragraphs, headings, tables, tabs and line breaks.
+  The importer stores these view objects under the account's erasable object prefix.
+* Added owner-private APIs for summary/news/evidence and paged workbook views, plus an audited
+  download that contains only the five recognized client deliverables. The original source ZIP and
+  internal-only files are never returned by the download API. The account import panel now opens
+  these views and downloads that client-only archive; imports still display `parity pending`.
+* Added source-view unit coverage and a database-backed API test for paging and internal-file
+  withholding. Focused backend checks: 19 passed. Targeted web checks: typecheck, ESLint and 3
+  parity UI tests passed. OpenAPI snapshot, generated client and route-policy catalog checks pass.
+  The database-backed API suite was attempted but could not initialize because the local PostgreSQL
+  test role has no password configured in this session.
+* Limits: source views expose the shipped content, not normalized/rebuilt output. Canonical query
+  execution, workspace-specific jobs/people/ranking transforms, generated deliverables, chat/Deep
+  integration and all-workspace golden acceptance remain outstanding. The two BD Jobs description
+  cell differences remain unresolved.
+
+## 2026-11-01: conservative canonical Ask results
+
+* Ask now resolves one unambiguous supported RESTORE query against the latest owner-visible
+  workspace import and computes its complete result set from the corresponding typed workbook
+  table. It uses no expected answer numbers from RESTORE and skips provider/key resolution for this
+  deterministic path. Strict zero is reported before a result with the final predicate relaxed.
+* The compiler carries explicit job entity scope across queries for the same source sheet. The
+  Platform Ranking query reports rank groups directly from the imported ranking sheet, without
+  using RESTORE's expected list as output. Waters' additional pre-close count, date-window semantics
+  and other unsupported, ambiguous or truncated queries stay on the existing Ask route.
+* Synthetic API coverage uses a deliberately false declared answer, verifies the imported-row count
+  and labeled strict-zero/relaxed result, and proves a model provider is not resolved. Focused
+  import/Ask/parity and repair tests passed (903); the account purge suite passed (25). The tenant
+  isolation matrix passed (564). A 201-test recovery set covering every failure from the
+  repository-wide run passed after the import repository/policy, deterministic table IDs, injected
+  clock, static guard and test-fixture fixes. The full run itself reported 7,436 passed, 7 skipped,
+  1 xfailed and 14 failures before those fixes; it has not been rerun end to end. Full frontend unit
+  tests passed (294), as did typecheck, ESLint and the production build. The OpenAPI snapshot/client
+  is regenerated after adding response-model descriptions.
+* Full legacy parity is still not green: four BD deliverables match the isolated RESTORE replay,
+  while the Jobs workbook still differs in two `Full description` cells. Other workspaces have not
+  been regenerated and compared, and Deep mode is not connected to imports.
